## Filling the pool

The provider claims from the pool, and falls back to creating a subscription
itself when the pool is empty and `billing_scope` is set. That fallback is the
slow, rate-limited path — it keeps an apply from failing, it is not a refill
strategy. Keep the pool stocked out of band instead: from cron, a scheduled
pipeline, anything that drops subscriptions into the pool management group.
With the Azure CLI:

{{ codefile "shell" "examples/refill-pool.sh" }}

The identity running this needs the billing role that can create subscriptions,
plus Management Group Contributor on the pool group.
